1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,374
A grainy black-and-white screen.

2
00:00:02,714 --> 00:00:04,688
A Navy targeting camera, locked onto

3
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:06,238
something over the Atlantic.

4
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:08,726
For years, clips like this were rumors.

5
00:00:09,066 --> 00:00:09,625
Leaks.

6
00:00:09,965 --> 00:00:11,163
Copies of copies.

7
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:14,028
Then, in April 2020, the Department of

8
00:00:14,048 --> 00:00:15,935
Defense did something unusual.

9
00:00:16,505 --> 00:00:18,301
It released three of these videos.

10
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:19,692
Officially.

11
00:00:20,275 --> 00:00:22,310
And it said the objects in them were still

12
00:00:23,268 --> 00:00:24,381
unidentified.

13
00:00:25,301 --> 00:00:27,399
So what do those three videos actually

14
00:00:27,419 --> 00:00:27,678
show?

15
00:00:28,148 --> 00:00:29,949
What did the government say about them?

16
00:00:30,419 --> 00:00:32,049
And what has it figured out since?

17
00:00:32,619 --> 00:00:33,892
Let's open the file.

18
00:00:40,219 --> 00:00:40,985
Three clips.

19
00:00:41,325 --> 00:00:42,225
Two oceans.

20
00:00:42,565 --> 00:00:43,667
A decade apart.

21
00:00:44,288 --> 00:00:47,225
The first is from November 14, 2004.

22
00:00:47,565 --> 00:00:49,701
The USS Nimitz carrier strike group is

23
00:00:49,721 --> 00:00:51,574
training off Southern California.

24
00:00:51,914 --> 00:00:54,520
According to CBS News, about 100 miles

25
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,110
southwest of San Diego.

26
00:00:56,679 --> 00:00:58,554
According to his later testimony,

27
00:00:58,574 --> 00:01:00,965
Commander David Fravor led a flight of two

28
00:01:00,985 --> 00:01:03,146
Navy jets sent to check out an unknown

29
00:01:03,166 --> 00:01:03,605
contact.

30
00:01:04,176 --> 00:01:06,532
According to Fravor, he saw a small white

31
00:01:06,552 --> 00:01:08,270
object, shaped like a Tic Tac.

32
00:01:08,690 --> 00:01:09,569
No wings.

33
00:01:09,989 --> 00:01:10,936
No rotors.

34
00:01:11,506 --> 00:01:14,089
He also says the cruiser USS Princeton had

35
00:01:14,109 --> 00:01:16,567
been tracking objects like this on radar

36
00:01:16,587 --> 00:01:18,984
for about two weeks, dropping from very

37
00:01:19,004 --> 00:01:19,851
high altitude.

38
00:01:20,191 --> 00:01:22,369
That radar data has not been publicly

39
00:01:22,389 --> 00:01:22,904
released.

40
00:01:23,474 --> 00:01:25,648
Fravor says a second crew went up later

41
00:01:25,668 --> 00:01:27,841
that day, and filmed something with the

42
00:01:27,861 --> 00:01:29,472
jet's infrared targeting pod.

43
00:01:29,812 --> 00:01:31,219
That clip has no sound.

44
00:01:31,559 --> 00:01:33,552
It became known as FLIR1.

45
00:01:34,122 --> 00:01:36,673
The other two videos come from January

46
00:01:36,693 --> 00:01:37,011
2015.

47
00:01:37,351 --> 00:01:39,235
A different carrier group, the USS

48
00:01:39,255 --> 00:01:41,531
Theodore Roosevelt, training off the East

49
00:01:41,551 --> 00:01:41,867
Coast.

50
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:44,742
Those two clips got the names GIMBAL, and

51
00:01:44,762 --> 00:01:45,138
GOFAST.

52
00:01:45,478 --> 00:01:47,368
The Navy has said both were recorded

53
00:01:47,388 --> 00:01:48,853
during that training period.

54
00:01:49,423 --> 00:01:51,407
Before we go further, let's learn to read

55
00:01:51,427 --> 00:01:51,944
the screen.

56
00:01:52,284 --> 00:01:54,498
Because almost every argument about these

57
00:01:54,518 --> 00:01:56,405
videos comes down to these numbers.

58
00:01:56,975 --> 00:01:58,072
This is GOFAST.

59
00:01:58,412 --> 00:02:00,600
The camera is pointed down at the ocean,

60
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,421
and it's tracking a small object.

61
00:02:02,991 --> 00:02:04,701
Here, the jet's own altitude.

62
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:06,762
About 25,000 feet.

63
00:02:07,102 --> 00:02:09,091
Here, the camera's angle, pointing down

64
00:02:09,111 --> 00:02:10,018
below the horizon.

65
00:02:10,358 --> 00:02:11,700
And here, RNG.

66
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,098
The range to the object, in nautical

67
00:02:14,118 --> 00:02:14,444
miles.

68
00:02:15,014 --> 00:02:16,874
Keep those three numbers in mind.

69
00:02:17,344 --> 00:02:18,339
They'll matter later.

70
00:02:19,159 --> 00:02:21,521
For years, nobody outside the military was

71
00:02:21,541 --> 00:02:23,109
supposed to see any of this.

72
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:26,526
But according to a Pentagon briefing card

73
00:02:26,546 --> 00:02:28,929
later released under the Freedom of

74
00:02:28,949 --> 00:02:31,745
Information Act, a copy of the 2004 video

75
00:02:31,765 --> 00:02:33,531
was posted online in 2007.

76
00:02:33,871 --> 00:02:34,893
Without permission.

77
00:02:35,463 --> 00:02:38,074
On December 16, 2017, The New York Times

78
00:02:38,094 --> 00:02:40,770
published a story about a secret Pentagon

79
00:02:40,790 --> 00:02:43,467
program that had looked into reports like

80
00:02:43,487 --> 00:02:43,861
these.

81
00:02:44,201 --> 00:02:45,634
With it came two videos.

82
00:02:45,974 --> 00:02:47,637
FLIR1, and GIMBAL.

83
00:02:48,207 --> 00:02:50,441
That same month, a private company called

84
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,531
To The Stars Academy put them out too.

85
00:02:52,871 --> 00:02:54,901
A third clip, GOFAST, surfaced a few

86
00:02:54,921 --> 00:02:55,642
months later.

87
00:02:56,212 --> 00:02:58,401
The Pentagon later said those two 2015

88
00:02:58,421 --> 00:03:00,377
clips reached the press through an

89
00:03:00,397 --> 00:03:01,597
unauthorized release.

90
00:03:01,937 --> 00:03:04,187
And the Navy, it said, had no information

91
00:03:04,207 --> 00:03:06,290
on how they were released into general

92
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:06,954
circulation.

93
00:03:07,524 --> 00:03:10,106
The Times reported that the program had

94
00:03:10,126 --> 00:03:11,240
cost $22 million.

95
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,692
The Pentagon's own description is much

96
00:03:13,712 --> 00:03:14,197
narrower.

97
00:03:14,537 --> 00:03:16,556
It says the effort studied foreign

98
00:03:16,576 --> 00:03:18,775
aerospace threats, and ended in 2012.

99
00:03:19,345 --> 00:03:21,125
So now the videos were everywhere.

100
00:03:21,595 --> 00:03:23,574
But nobody official had confirmed they

101
00:03:23,594 --> 00:03:24,100
were real.

102
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,416
That silence ended in September 2019.

103
00:03:28,035 --> 00:03:30,008
A Navy spokesman, Joseph Gradisher,

104
00:03:30,028 --> 00:03:30,748
confirmed it.

105
00:03:31,088 --> 00:03:33,312
The three videos were copies of official

106
00:03:33,332 --> 00:03:34,041
Navy footage.

107
00:03:34,611 --> 00:03:36,977
He said the Navy considered the objects

108
00:03:36,997 --> 00:03:37,772
unidentified.

109
00:03:38,355 --> 00:03:40,480
And that they had entered Navy training

110
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:40,865
ranges.

111
00:03:41,435 --> 00:03:43,348
He also pushed back on one claim.

112
00:03:43,688 --> 00:03:45,715
The private company had said the videos

113
00:03:45,735 --> 00:03:47,446
were approved for public release.

114
00:03:47,786 --> 00:03:49,614
According to Gradisher, they were not.

115
00:03:50,184 --> 00:03:52,732
Then came April 27, 2020.

116
00:03:53,072 --> 00:03:55,313
The Department of Defense put out a short

117
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:57,575
statement, and posted the three files for

118
00:03:57,595 --> 00:03:58,622
anyone to download.

119
00:03:59,192 --> 00:04:00,705
Notice the word it used.

120
00:04:01,287 --> 00:04:02,363
Unclassified.

121
00:04:02,946 --> 00:04:05,087
These weren't secret documents being

122
00:04:05,107 --> 00:04:05,867
declassified.

123
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:08,314
They were videos that had already leaked,

124
00:04:08,334 --> 00:04:09,661
now released on the record.

125
00:04:10,231 --> 00:04:11,579
Why release them at all?

126
00:04:12,049 --> 00:04:14,115
The Pentagon said it wanted to clear up

127
00:04:14,135 --> 00:04:16,039
any misconceptions about whether the

128
00:04:16,059 --> 00:04:16,948
footage was real.

129
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:19,719
And on what the objects were, it gave one

130
00:04:19,739 --> 00:04:20,099
answer.

131
00:04:20,681 --> 00:04:22,440
They remain unidentified.

132
00:04:23,459 --> 00:04:26,181
In 2025, a Freedom of Information Act

133
00:04:26,201 --> 00:04:28,700
request pried loose 264 pages of a

134
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:31,664
Pentagon spokesperson's emails about the

135
00:04:31,684 --> 00:04:32,257
release.

136
00:04:32,597 --> 00:04:33,716
Partly redacted.

137
00:04:34,536 --> 00:04:36,406
Videos are one kind of evidence.

138
00:04:36,876 --> 00:04:37,883
People are another.

139
00:04:38,502 --> 00:04:40,624
In July 2023, a House Oversight

140
00:04:40,644 --> 00:04:42,696
subcommittee held a hearing on

141
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:44,975
unidentified anomalous phenomena.

142
00:04:45,315 --> 00:04:46,833
Every witness was sworn in.

143
00:04:47,404 --> 00:04:49,737
Fravor, now retired, repeated his account

144
00:04:49,757 --> 00:04:50,368
under oath.

145
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:52,817
He described a white Tic Tac object, and

146
00:04:52,837 --> 00:04:54,893
said his flight got within about half a

147
00:04:54,913 --> 00:04:55,479
mile of it.

148
00:04:56,049 --> 00:04:58,231
In his account, the object turned toward

149
00:04:58,251 --> 00:04:59,167
his jet, climbed,

150
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:01,801
and then accelerated away, and was gone.

151
00:05:02,372 --> 00:05:04,614
His wingman that day, Alex Dietrich, did

152
00:05:04,634 --> 00:05:05,293
not testify.

153
00:05:05,633 --> 00:05:08,046
But in a 2021 television interview, she

154
00:05:08,066 --> 00:05:10,603
said the object moved with no predictable

155
00:05:10,623 --> 00:05:11,290
trajectory.

156
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:14,120
Then there's Ryan Graves, a former pilot

157
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:16,400
with Strike Fighter Squadron 11, the Red

158
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:16,856
Rippers.

159
00:05:17,196 --> 00:05:19,424
In his written testimony, he says GIMBAL

160
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:21,055
was recorded by his squadron.

161
00:05:21,625 --> 00:05:24,310
In 2019, he told The New York Times that

162
00:05:24,330 --> 00:05:26,881
pilots in his squadron saw unexplained

163
00:05:26,901 --> 00:05:29,383
objects almost every day, for months.

164
00:05:29,953 --> 00:05:31,954
In his statement for the hearing, Graves

165
00:05:31,974 --> 00:05:33,621
passed on another pilot's report.

166
00:05:33,961 --> 00:05:36,221
A dark gray cube, inside a clear sphere,

167
00:05:36,241 --> 00:05:37,303
off Virginia Beach.

168
00:05:37,873 --> 00:05:39,889
And the third witness, David Grusch, a

169
00:05:39,909 --> 00:05:42,033
former senior intelligence officer, made

170
00:05:42,053 --> 00:05:42,997
the biggest claim.

171
00:05:43,337 --> 00:05:45,263
He said he had been told of a secret

172
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:47,047
program to recover crashed craft.

173
00:05:47,617 --> 00:05:49,039
Here's the key detail.

174
00:05:49,622 --> 00:05:51,892
He said his testimony was based on what

175
00:05:51,912 --> 00:05:52,831
others told him.

176
00:05:53,251 --> 00:05:55,443
And the Pentagon says it has found no

177
00:05:55,463 --> 00:05:57,654
verifiable evidence for programs like

178
00:05:57,674 --> 00:05:57,953
that.

179
00:05:58,773 --> 00:06:00,426
So, what does the government's own

180
00:06:00,446 --> 00:06:01,065
analysis say?

181
00:06:01,685 --> 00:06:04,130
In June 2021, the Office of the Director

182
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:06,471
of National Intelligence published its

183
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,950
first public assessment.

184
00:06:08,290 --> 00:06:10,814
It looked at 144 reports from U.S.

185
00:06:10,834 --> 00:06:12,235
government sources.

186
00:06:12,805 --> 00:06:13,763
It could explain

187
00:06:14,346 --> 00:06:14,867
one.

188
00:06:15,449 --> 00:06:17,154
A large, deflating balloon.

189
00:06:18,074 --> 00:06:19,775
The report had other numbers worth

190
00:06:19,795 --> 00:06:20,179
knowing.

191
00:06:20,519 --> 00:06:22,917
80 of the reports involved more than one

192
00:06:22,937 --> 00:06:23,339
sensor.

193
00:06:23,679 --> 00:06:26,113
In eighteen incidents, observers reported

194
00:06:26,133 --> 00:06:27,669
unusual movement or flight

195
00:06:27,689 --> 00:06:28,626
characteristics.

196
00:06:28,966 --> 00:06:31,199
And pilots reported eleven near-misses.

197
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:34,122
A year later, in July 2020-two, the

198
00:06:34,142 --> 00:06:36,698
Pentagon created a dedicated office to

199
00:06:36,718 --> 00:06:37,512
investigate.

200
00:06:37,852 --> 00:06:40,267
The All-domain Anomaly Resolution Office.

201
00:06:40,607 --> 00:06:41,261
AARO.

202
00:06:41,601 --> 00:06:44,792
Its first big count, published in early

203
00:06:44,812 --> 00:06:48,004
2023, brought the total to 510 reports,

204
00:06:48,024 --> 00:06:49,898
including 366 new ones.

205
00:06:50,468 --> 00:06:53,938
Of those 366, 163 were balloons or

206
00:06:53,958 --> 00:06:55,272
balloon-like.

207
00:06:55,612 --> 00:06:57,610
26 were drones, or drone-like.

208
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:58,940
Six were clutter.

209
00:06:59,410 --> 00:07:02,342
And 171 were still uncharacterized.

210
00:07:02,912 --> 00:07:05,041
Since then, analysts have worked through

211
00:07:05,061 --> 00:07:06,116
hundreds more cases.

212
00:07:06,456 --> 00:07:08,675
And one of the famous Navy videos now has

213
00:07:08,695 --> 00:07:09,713
an official answer.

214
00:07:10,282 --> 00:07:12,486
Remember those three numbers on the GOFAST

215
00:07:12,506 --> 00:07:12,856
screen?

216
00:07:13,326 --> 00:07:14,578
Here's where they come in.

217
00:07:15,148 --> 00:07:17,507
If you know how high the jet is, which way

218
00:07:17,527 --> 00:07:19,715
the camera points, and how far away the

219
00:07:19,735 --> 00:07:21,811
object is, you can work out where the

220
00:07:21,831 --> 00:07:22,773
object really is.

221
00:07:23,343 --> 00:07:26,573
In 2023, a NASA study team did that math.

222
00:07:26,993 --> 00:07:29,786
It put the object at about 13,000 feet.

223
00:07:30,369 --> 00:07:31,738
Not skimming the water.

224
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,228
Halfway between the jet and the sea.

225
00:07:34,798 --> 00:07:35,655
And its speed?

226
00:07:36,175 --> 00:07:37,667
About 40 mph.

227
00:07:38,007 --> 00:07:39,984
Roughly what the wind does at that height.

228
00:07:40,554 --> 00:07:42,158
So why does it look so fast?

229
00:07:42,678 --> 00:07:44,632
Because the camera is on a jet doing

230
00:07:44,652 --> 00:07:46,057
hundreds of miles an hour.

231
00:07:46,397 --> 00:07:47,942
The background rushes past.

232
00:07:48,412 --> 00:07:49,909
The object barely moves.

233
00:07:50,249 --> 00:07:51,394
It's called parallax.

234
00:07:51,964 --> 00:07:54,334
In November 2024, AARO's director, Jon

235
00:07:54,354 --> 00:07:56,724
Kosloski, told a Senate Armed Services

236
00:07:56,744 --> 00:07:59,366
subcommittee the office had assessed, with

237
00:07:59,386 --> 00:08:01,882
high confidence, that the object was not

238
00:08:01,902 --> 00:08:03,642
actually close to the water.

239
00:08:04,213 --> 00:08:06,871
Less than three months later, in February

240
00:08:06,891 --> 00:08:09,614
2025, AARO published its formal resolution

241
00:08:09,634 --> 00:08:10,398
of the case.

242
00:08:10,738 --> 00:08:11,824
Same altitude.

243
00:08:12,164 --> 00:08:13,368
Same explanation.

244
00:08:13,708 --> 00:08:15,980
It said the object was consistent with a

245
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,329
small airborne object, such as a balloon,

246
00:08:18,349 --> 00:08:18,960
or a drone.

247
00:08:19,529 --> 00:08:21,650
AARO was also clear about the limits.

248
00:08:21,990 --> 00:08:24,287
The original file and its data were lost.

249
00:08:24,627 --> 00:08:27,031
It worked from the public 34-second clip.

250
00:08:27,371 --> 00:08:29,679
And it never identified exactly what the

251
00:08:29,699 --> 00:08:30,318
object was.

252
00:08:30,889 --> 00:08:32,621
Critics have pointed out other gaps.

253
00:08:32,961 --> 00:08:35,342
Writing in the Daily Grail, one noted that

254
00:08:35,362 --> 00:08:37,458
AARO didn't interview the pilots, and

255
00:08:37,478 --> 00:08:39,402
didn't estimate the object's size.

256
00:08:39,971 --> 00:08:41,287
What about the other two?

257
00:08:41,869 --> 00:08:43,441
Here, the record gets thin.

258
00:08:44,011 --> 00:08:46,120
For GIMBAL, some independent analysts

259
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:48,421
argue the shape is infrared glare from a

260
00:08:48,441 --> 00:08:50,779
distant jet engine, and that the rotation

261
00:08:50,799 --> 00:08:52,447
comes from the camera itself.

262
00:08:52,787 --> 00:08:53,985
Others dispute that.

263
00:08:54,455 --> 00:08:55,349
It's a theory.

264
00:08:55,689 --> 00:08:57,873
No government body has endorsed it, or

265
00:08:57,893 --> 00:08:58,626
ruled it out.

266
00:08:59,197 --> 00:09:01,821
And FLIR1, the Tic Tac video, has no

267
00:09:01,841 --> 00:09:03,878
official explanation either.

268
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,637
Not from the Navy.

269
00:09:06,058 --> 00:09:07,224
Not from AARO.

270
00:09:08,143 --> 00:09:09,448
Which brings us to now.

271
00:09:10,068 --> 00:09:12,805
In 2026, the release of government UAP

272
00:09:12,825 --> 00:09:14,546
records picked up speed.

273
00:09:14,886 --> 00:09:17,278
According to The Washington Post, the

274
00:09:17,298 --> 00:09:20,016
president directed agencies in February to

275
00:09:20,036 --> 00:09:22,623
identify and declassify their UAP files.

276
00:09:23,194 --> 00:09:25,295
In May, the Pentagon launched a public

277
00:09:25,315 --> 00:09:27,471
website for releasing those records, in

278
00:09:27,491 --> 00:09:27,918
batches.

279
00:09:28,258 --> 00:09:31,764
And in July, AARO's latest annual report

280
00:09:31,784 --> 00:09:35,291
counted 319 new cases, and 370 resolved.

281
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,252
Every one of those resolved cases had an

282
00:09:38,272 --> 00:09:40,664
ordinary explanation, according to AARO.

283
00:09:41,234 --> 00:09:42,827
